{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"111482","commit":"87d90c37479abe89bfb8d696d44822da5d1373f6","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The variable `allValuesNull` is computed with `anyMatch(Block::areAllValuesNull)`, which returns `true` if *any* block is entirely null. The name implies \"all values are null\" (i.e., every block is all-nulls), but the logic is \"at least one block is all-nulls.\" If the intent is to skip chunked processing when *any* input column is entirely null (since most aggregations would yield null), the logic is correct but the name is misleading. If the intent is \"all values across all columns are null,\" then `allMatch` should be used instead. Please clarify the intent and rename accordingly (e.g., `anyBlockAllNull` vs `allBlocksAllNull`).","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/AbstractAggregationTestCase.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/AbstractAggregationTestCase.java-18934:18969,19380:19393-19131:19294,19424:19512,19570:19634,19953:20041,20155:20178,20180:20202","promptId":"#1S67X","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/AbstractAggregationTestCase.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/AbstractAggregationTestCase.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":18934,"endPos":18969,"startLine":440,"startLineOffset":57,"endLine":440,"endLineOffset":92,"length":36},{"pos":19380,"endPos":19393,"startLine":447,"startLineOffset":108,"endLine":447,"endLineOffset":121,"length":14}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":19131,"endPos":19294,"startLine":448,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":450,"endLineOffset":47,"length":164},{"pos":19424,"endPos":19512,"startLine":453,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":453,"endLineOffset":100,"length":89},{"pos":19570,"endPos":19634,"startLine":454,"startLineOffset":57,"endLine":454,"endLineOffset":121,"length":65},{